This solution uses dynamic programming to compute the sum of distances for all possible permutations of the parent sequence \( P \). It constructs the tree for each permutation and checks if the path from \( u_i \) to \( v_i \) exists in the tree. The time complexity is \( O(N \cdot Q \cdot (N-1)!) \) due to the factorial number of permutations and the need to check each permutation. The space complexity is \( O(N^2) \) for storing the adjacency list and distances.

